cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Arithmetic convolution fields — reproduction packets
message: >-
  If you use a packet from this repository, cite the paper in that
  directory and this archive. Each paper directory is self-contained and
  can be cited on its own; the paper's own reproducibility section names
  the release its figures were computed in.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Youngrok
    country: KR
abstract: >-
  Reproduction packets for papers on the fluctuation structure of
  convolution sums of arithmetic functions, built around
  C(N) = sum Lambda(n) mu(N-n) and Z(N) = C(N)/sqrt(V(N)). One directory
  per paper, each holding the source, the compiled PDF, every script the
  paper cites, the output those scripts produced, and — where the paper
  has one — a Lean 4 development with its axiom report. A packet is
  closed under what it consumes: no script reads a file that is not
  present, and no import resolves outside the directory. What is
  machine-checked is in every case the finite identities a proof runs
  on, never the theorem the paper argues for; each paper says where its
  formalisation stops and why. No paper here has had a reading by a
  subject expert, and each says so.
keywords:
  - analytic number theory
  - singular series
  - Moebius function
  - von Mangoldt function
  - Bombieri-Vinogradov
  - variance
  - permutation test
  - Lean
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: https://github.com/soke91/arithmetic-convolution-fields
